== Effects ==
* Grants [[homing tears]].

== Notes ==
* {{dlc+|r+}} This item has a 1% chance to drop when defeating {{e|Rag Mega}}.{{dlc-}}
* This item replaces Isaac's regular white aura with a dimmer purple one which lowers visibility in {{curse|darkness}}.

== Synergies ==
* {{I|Abyss}}: When Isaac uses Abyss to absorb Spoon Bender it turns into a purple locust that homes in on enemies while it is charging forward.
* {{i|Aquarius|r}}: Trail of creep is purple and homes in on enemies.
* {{c|Azazel}} / {{i|Brimstone}} / {{c|Tainted Azazel|r}}  / {{i|Technology}} / {{i|Technology 2}} / {{i|Tech X}}: Beams curve toward enemies.
** {{c|Azazel}} requires about 8.8 range in order for the homing effect to function.
* {{i|Compound Fracture}} / {{i|Cricket's Body}} / {{i|The Parasite}}: Tears and split tears are homing.
* {{i|Dr. Fetus}}: The bombs slide towards enemies.
* {{i|Marked}}: Tears will travel in the direction of the cross-hairs until close enough to home in on an enemy.
* {{i|Mom's Knife}}: The knife curves towards enemies.

== Interactions ==
* {{I|Anti-Gravity}}: Tears can track enemies while frozen in place, once one comes close enough.
* {{i|Epic Fetus|a}}: Cursor slides towards enemies.
* {{i|Eye of the Occult}}: Tears home in on enemies when not being maneuvered.
* {{i|The Ludovico Technique}}: The tear will attempt to home towards a single target, even if it hits a different enemy on its way there, making it difficult to control.
** {{dlc|r}} The changes to homing tears make it nearly impossible to maintain control of the shot while it's near an enemy.
* {{i|Technology Zero}}: The electricity is unaffected.

